ekeeping units of the game. This cannot be changed later.

Calendar-based is the classic OpenTTD experience, with a year consisting of 12 months, and each month having 28-31 days.

In Wallclock-based time, cargo production and financials are instead based on one-minute increments, which is about as long as a 30 day month takes in Calendar-based mode. These are grouped into 12-minute periods, equivalent to a year in Calendar-based mode.

In either mode there is always a classic calendar, which is used for introduction dates of vehicles, houses, and other infrastructureCalendar	WallclockMinutes per year: �~Choose the number of minutes in a calendar year. The default is 12 minutes. Set to 0 to stop calendar time from changing. Increasing the length of the calendar year slows down the introduction of vehicles, houses, and other infrastructure. It does not affect vehicle speed or economic simulation, except for inflation. This setting is only available when using wallclock timekeeping0 (calendar time frozen) Scale town cargo production: 6Scale the cargo production of towns by this percentage$Scale industry cargo production: ;Scale the cargo production of industries by this percentage%(Outohernuwe voertuig as hy oud raak: �As dit geaktiveer is, word 'n voertuig wat naby die einde van sy werkslewe kom outomaties vervang, wanneer die hernu voorwaardes vervul is.3Vervang voertuig outomaties na  maksimum leeftydHRelatiewe ouderdom waneer voertuie herweeg moet word ver outo-vervanging maand␀␀␀e voor maand␀␀␀e later2Outohernuwe minimum vereisde geld vir hernuwe: ^Minimale bedrag geld wat in die bank moet bly, voor die oorweging van motor-vernuwing voertuieTyd wat fout boodskap wys: iTydsduur vir die vertoning van foutboodskappe. Kritiese foutboodskappe word nie outomaties toegemaak nie.wys sleutel-leidraad: ��Tydsduur voor nutswenke vertoon words as die muis oor koppelvlakelemente gehou word. Alternatiewelik kan die nutswenke ook aan die regter-muisknoppie verbind word indien die stelling na 0 gestel word.Sweef vir  sekonde␀␀␀sRegsklik*Toon stadsbevolking in die naametiket: @Vertoon die bevolking van 'n stad in die naametiket op die kaartDikte van lyn in grafieke: �Wydte van kaartlyne. A dun lyn is meer akkuraat om te lees, maar 'n dikker lyn is makliker om te sien en te onderskei van ander lyne.:Toon die NewGRF se naam in die bou van voertuie skerm: mVoeg 'n lyn by die ven