mpany's performance during the period compared to the previous periodConstruction: 7Play sound on successful constructions or other actionsButton clicks: Beep when clicking buttonsDisasters/accidents: -Play sound effects of accidents and disastersVehicles: Play sound effects of vehiclesAmbient: 6Play ambient sounds of landscape, industries and towns)Maximum number of trains per company: 0Maximum number of trains that a company can have0Maximum number of road vehicles per company: 7Maximum number of road vehicles that a company can have+Maximum number of aircraft per company: 2Maximum number of aircraft that a company can have(Maximum number of ships per company: /Maximum number of ships that a company can have Disable trains for computer: LEnabling this setting makes building trains impossible for a computer player'Disable road vehicles for computer: SEnabling this setting makes building road vehicles impossible for a computer player"Disable aircraft for computer: NEnabling this setting makes building aircraft impossible for a computer playerDisable ships for computer: KEnabling this setting makes building ships impossible for a computer playerAllow AIs in multiplayer: =Allow AI computer players to participate in multiplayer games*#opcodes before scripts are suspended: FMaximum number of computation steps that a script can take in one turn Max memory usage per script: yHow much memory a single script may consume before it's forcibly terminated. This may need to be increased for large maps MiB&Service intervals are in percents: �When enabled, vehicles try to service when their reliability drops by a given percentage of the maximum reliability.

For example, if a vehicle's maximum reliability is 90% and the service interval is 20%, the vehicle will try to service when it reaches 72% reliability(Default service interval for trains: nSet the default service interval for new rail vehicles, if no explicit service interval is set for the vehicle/Default service interval for road vehicles: nSet the default service interval for new road vehicles, if no explicit service interval is set for the vehicle*Default service interval for aircraft: iSet the default service interval for new aircraft, if no explicit service interval is set for the vehicle'Default service interval for ships: fSet the default service interval for new ships, if no explicit service interval is set for the vehicle Day␀␀␀s Minute␀␀␀s %Disabled2Disable servicing when breakdowns set to none: DWhen enabled, vehicles do not get serviced if they cannot break downFLoading speed penalty for trains that are longer than the station: �When enabled, trains which are too long for the station load more slowly than a train which fits the station. This setting does not affect pathfindingEnable wagon speed limits: WWhen enabled, also use speed limits of wagons for deciding the maximum speed of a trainDisable electric rails: gEnabling this setting disables the requirement to electrify tracks to make electric engines run on them1Arrival of first vehicle at player's station: LDisplay a newspaper when the first vehicle arrives at a new player's station5Arrival of first vehicle at competitor's station: PDisplay a newspaper when the first vehicle arrives at a new competitor's stationAccidents / disasters: 5Display a newspaper when accidents or disasters occur'Accidents of competitor's vehicles: :Display a newspaper about crashed vehicles for competitorsCompany information: XDisplay a newspaper when a new company starts, or when companies are risking to bankruptOpening of industries: ,Display a newspaper when new industries openClosing of industries: .Display a newspaper when industries close downEconomy changes: 3Display a newspaper about global changes to economy;Production changes of industries served by the company: cDisplay a newspaper when the production level of industries change, which are served by the company=Production changes of industries served by competitor(s): gDisplay a newspaper when the production level of industries change, which are served by the competitors&Other industry production changes: vDisplay a newspaper when the production level of industries change, which are not served by the company or competitors/Advice / information on company's vehicles: 1Display messages about vehicles needing attentionNew vehicles: =Display a newspaper when a new vehicle type becomes available Changes to cargo acceptance: CDisplay messages about stations changing acceptance of some cargoesГрантсем: 0Display a newspaper about subsidy related eventsGeneral information: nDisplay newspaper about general events, such as purchase of exclusive rights or funding of road reconstructionСӳнтер
