* Large airplanes always have a risk of crashing when landing on small airportsNone*ReducedNormalCAllow level crossings with roads or rails owned by competitors: LAllow construction of level crossings on roads or rails owned by competitors;Allow drive-through road stops on roads owned by towns: FAllow construction of drive-through road stops on roads owned by townsAAllow drive-through road stops on roads owned by competitors: PAllow construction of drive-through road stops on roads owned by other companies@Changing this setting is not possible when there are vehiclesInfrastructure maintenance: �When enabled, infrastructure causes maintenance costs. The cost grows over-proportional with the network size, thus affecting bigger companies more than smaller onesStarting company colour: &Choose starting colour for the company&Starting company secondary colour: SChoose starting secondary colour for the company, if using a NewGRF that enables itAirports never expire: [Enabling this setting makes each airport type stay available forever after its introductionWarn if vehicle is lost: RTrigger messages about vehicles unable to find a path to their ordered destinationReview vehicles' orders: �Lसक्षम होने पर वाहनों के निर्देशों की आवधिक जाँच की जाती है, और कुछ सुस्पष्ट मामलों का पता चलते ही एक संदेश द्वारा बताया जाता है।नहीं!Yes, but exclude stopped vehiclesOf all vehicles+Warn if a vehicle's income is negative: [When enabled, a news message gets sent when a vehicle has not made any profit within a year]When enabled, a news message gets sent when a vehicle has not made any profit within a period%Warn if a vehicle is getting old: DWhen enabled, a news message gets sent when a vehicle is getting oldVehicles never expire: RWhen enabled, all vehicle models remain available forever after their introductionTimekeeping: �LSelect the timekeeping units of the game. This cannot be changed later.

Calendar-based is the classic OpenTTD experience, with a year consisting of 12 months, and each month having 28-31 days.

In Wallclock-based time, cargo production and financials are instead based on one-minute increments, which is about as long as a 30 day month takes in Calendar-based mode. These are grouped into 12-minute periods, equivalent to a year in Calendar-based mode.

In either mode there is always a classic calendar, which is used for introduction dates of vehicles, houses, and other infrastructureCalendar	WallclockMinutes per year: �~Choose the number of minutes in a calendar year. The default is 12 minutes. Set to 0 to stop calendar time from changing. Increasing the length of the calendar year slows down the introduction of vehicles, houses, and other infrastructure. It does not affect vehicle speed or economic simulation, except for inflation. This setting is only available when using wallclock timekeeping0 (calendar time frozen) Scale town cargo production: 6Scale the cargo production of towns by this percentage$Scale industry cargo production: ;Scale the cargo production of industries by this percentage%'Autorenew vehicle when it gets old: sWhen enabled, a vehicle nearing its end of life gets automatically replaced when the renew conditions are fulfilled)Autorenew when vehicle is  maximum ageBRelative age when a vehicle should be considered for auto-renewing month␀␀␀s before month␀␀␀s after-Autorenew minimum needed money for renew: ^Minimal amount of money that must remain in the bank before considering auto-renewing vehiclesDuration of error message: ��लाल विंडो में त्रुटि संदेश प्रदर्शित करने की अवधि। ध्यान दें कि कुछ (महत्वपूर्ण) त्रुटि संदेश इस समय के बाद स्वचालित रूप से बंद नहीं होते हैं, लेकिन उन्हें मैन्युअल रूप से बंद किया जाना चाहिएShow tooltips: �Delay before tooltips are displayed when hovering the mouse over some interface element. Alternatively tooltips are bound to the right mouse button when this value is set to 0"Hover for  millisecond␀␀␀sRight click0Show town population in the town name label: 9Display the population of towns in their label on the map!Thickness of lines in graphs: �Width of the line in the graphs. A thin line is more precisely readable, a thicker line is easier to see and colours are easier to distinguish7Show the NewGRF's name in the build vehicle window: \Add a line to the build vehicle window, showing which NewGRF the selected vehicle comes from@Show the cargoes the vehicles can carry in the list windows: VIf enabled, the vehicle's transportable load will appear above it in the vehicle listsLandscape: �Landscapes define basic gameplay scenarios with different cargoes and town growth requirements. NewGRF and Game Scripts allow finer control thoughLand generator: �The original generator depends on the base graphics set, and composes fixed landscape shapes. TerraGenesis is a Perlin noise based generator with finer control settingsOriginalTerraGenesisTerrain type: 9Choose the height of hills and mountains of the landscapeIndustry density: _Set how many industries should be generated and what level should be maintained during the game2Maximum distance from edge for Oil industries: ��Limit for how far from the map border oil refineries and oil rigs can be constructed. On island maps this ensures they are near the coast. On maps larger than 256 tiles, this value is scaled upSnow line height: ��Choose at what height snow starts in sub-arctic landscape. Snow also affects industry generation and town growth requirements. Can only be modified via Scenario Editor or is otherwise calculated via "snow coverage"Snow coverage: ��Choose the approximate amount of snow on the sub-arctic landscape. Snow also affects industry generation and town growth requirements. Only used during map generation. Sea level and coast tiles never have snow%Desert coverage: �Choose the approximate amount of desert on the tropical landscape. Desert also affects industry generation and town growth requirements. Only used during map generation%Roughness of terrain: �Choose the shape and number of hills. Smooth landscapes have fewer, wider hills, while rough landscapes have more, smaller hillsVery SmoothSmoothRough
