ward is enabled. 0 = no limit (as fast as your computer allows). Values below 100% slow the game down. The upper-limit depends on the specification of your computer and can vary depending on the game% normal game speed*No limit (as fast as your computer allows)News ticker: 'Play sound for summarised news messagesNewspaper: %Play sound upon display of newspapersEnd of year: End of period: sPlay sound at the end of a year summarising the company's performance during the year compared to the previous yearyPlay sound at the end of a period summarising the company's performance during the period compared to the previous periodConstruction: 7Play sound on successful constructions or other actionsButton clicks: Beep when clicking buttonsDisasters/accidents: -Play sound effects of accidents and disastersVehicles: Play sound effects of vehiclesAmbient: 6Play ambient sounds of landscape, industries and towns)Maximum number of trains per company: 0Maximum number of trains that a company can have0Maximum number of road vehicles per company: 7Maximum number of road vehicles that a company can have+Maximum number of aircraft per company: 2Maximum number of aircraft that a company can have(Maximum number of ships per company: /Maximum number of ships that a company can have Disable trains for computer: LEnabling this setting makes building trains impossible for a computer player'Disable road vehicles for computer: SEnabling this setting makes building road vehicles impossible for a computer player"Disable aircraft for computer: NEnabling this setting makes building aircraft impossible for a computer playerDisable ships for computer: KEnabling this setting makes building ships impossible for a computer playerAllow AIs in multiplayer: =Allow AI computer players to participate in multiplayer games*#opcodes before scripts are suspended: FMaximum number of computation steps that a script can take in one turn Max memory usage per script: yHow much memory a single script may consume before it's forcibly terminated. This may need to be increased for large maps MiB&Service intervals are in percents: �When enabled, vehicles try to service when their reliability drops by a given percentage of the maximum reliability.

